<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tujibids</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Banu Tujib, Tujibid dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tujibids were an Arab family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-march">Upper March of al-Andalus</a>, descended from the Yemeni tribe of Tujib, who replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a> as its leading lords in the 10th century. They governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calatayud">Calatayud</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daroca">Daroca</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, and after the caliphate collapsed they ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> of Zaragoza from 1018 until 1039, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hud">Banu Hud</a> overthrew them.</p></div>
